 **macOS 14 or later** (Apple Silicon and Intel) **and Linux** (x86_64 and arm64) — paste into Terminal:
 
 ```sh
-curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zoefix/agent-speed/main/install.sh | sh
+curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yooztech/agent-speed/main/install.sh | sh
 ```
 
 **Windows 10 / 11** (x64 and ARM64) — paste into PowerShell:
 
 ```powershell
-irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/zoefix/agent-speed/main/install.ps1 | iex
+irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/yooztech/agent-speed/main/install.ps1 | iex
 ```
 
 That's it. The installer downloads the latest release from GitHub, verifies its SHA-256 checksum, installs it and starts it. Run the same command again to update.
 
-On Linux the script installs the AppImage into `~/.local/share/agent-speed`, where it updates itself from inside the app, and adds Agent Speed to the application menu. It needs glibc 2.35 or later on x86_64 (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12 and newer) and 2.39 on arm64 (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13 and newer). The tray icon needs a StatusNotifierItem host: KDE Plasma has one; on GNOME, enable the AppIndicator extension (built into Ubuntu). Prefer a package? The [latest release](https://github.com/zoefix/agent-speed/releases/latest) also has a `.deb` (`sudo apt install ./agent-speed_*_amd64.deb`), checked with `SHA256SUMS-Linux-<arch>.txt`.
+Alternatively, on Windows download and run `AgentSpeed-Windows-x64-Setup.exe` or `AgentSpeed-Windows-arm64-Setup.exe` from the [latest release](https://github.com/yooztech/agent-speed/releases/latest). The installer is unsigned, so Microsoft Defender SmartScreen may warn before you can run it. Windows ZIP packages remain available on the same release page.
+
+On Linux the script installs the AppImage into `~/.local/share/agent-speed`, where it updates itself from inside the app, and adds Agent Speed to the application menu. It needs glibc 2.35 or later on x86_64 (Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12 and newer) and 2.39 on arm64 (Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13 and newer). The tray icon needs a StatusNotifierItem host: KDE Plasma has one; on GNOME, enable the AppIndicator extension (built into Ubuntu). Prefer a package? The [latest release](https://github.com/yooztech/agent-speed/releases/latest) also has a `.deb` (`sudo apt install ./agent-speed_*_amd64.deb`), checked with `SHA256SUMS-Linux-<arch>.txt`.
 
